UP.md`** — Full documentation with manual and automated setup instructions\n2. **`setup-git-server.sh`** — Script to configure the Git server on your machine\n3. **`demo-git-server.sh`** — Local demo to test the entire workflow\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**On your server machine:**\n```bash\nbash /app/setup-git-server.sh\nbash /app/start-web-server.sh\n```\n\n**On your client machine:**\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-project\ncd my-project\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html  # Returns: hello world\n```\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe post-receive hook automatically runs after each push and:\n1. Checks out the latest files from the git repo\n2. Syncs them to `/tmp/web-root` (web server directory)\n3. Makes them accessible via HTTP on port 8080\n\n## Test Locally First\n\nTo verify everything works before deploying:\n```bash\nbash /app/demo-git-server.sh\n```\n\nThis creates a complete working example in `/tmp` that you can test.","ttft_ms":5572,"type":"result","duration_ms":35337,"uuid":"3a4c78c9-ca2b-45d2-a54d-049fe55769e3","ttft_stream_ms":1120,"time_to_request_ms":91,"queued_turn_count":0}
